{W Triangulation W wins by triagulating his K over the sqs f4, e4, e5, turning
the move over to Bk} 1. Kf4 Ke8 (1... Kf7 2. Kf5 {and W has the oppositon}) 2.
Ke4 Kf8 3. Ke5 Kf7 (3... Ke8 4. Ke6 Kf8 5. f7 Kg7 6. Ke7 Kh7 7. f8=Q $4 {
would be stalemate} (7. Kf6 Kh8 8. f8=Q+ Kh7 9. Qg7#)) 4. Kf5 {and the BK must
give ground} Kf8 5. Kg6 *

